<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The Royal Reese's Blizzard: The Ultimate Peanut Butter Sensory Overdrive</h2>
    <p>For dedicated peanut butter purists, standard ice cream mix-ins often dilute the salty, roasted nut character with too much sugar and cold cream. The <strong>Royal Reese's® Peanut Butter Cup Blizzard® Treat</strong> solves that problem by turning the core into a pure peanut butter volcano. Beginning with Dairy Queen's vanilla soft serve whipped thoroughly with chopped Hershey's Reese's peanut butter cups, the crew fills a central vertical well with warm, liquified peanut butter sauce. Each spoonful transitions from cold chocolate-peanut candy crumbles to an intense, warm burst of rich, nutty peanut butter. Check out the complete lineup on <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard Treats</a> or view current nationwide pricing on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Comparing the Reese's Heavyweights</h2>
    <p>Deciding between the standard cup and the Royal edition comes down to flavor saturation:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Comparison Feature</th><th>Standard Reese's® Blizzard</th><th>Royal Reese's® Blizzard</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Starting Price</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49 (Mini)</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99 (Mini)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Small Baseline</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.49 (600 cal)</td><td class="price-cell">$4.99 (620 cal)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Center Injection</strong></td><td>None (fully blended throughout)</td><td>Warm, molten peanut butter topping core</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Peanut Butter Saturation</strong></td><td>Moderate, balanced by vanilla soft serve</td><td>Extremely concentrated salty-sweet core</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2>Calorie Context &amp; Mindful Sizing Recommendations</h2>
    <p>Packing 620 calories in a Small and scaling up to approximately 1,280 calories in the Large, the Royal Reese's is Dairy Queen's highest-calorie treat. To enjoy it without feeling overwhelmed:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The Mini ($3.99, ~400 cal):</strong> Ideal for a solo indulgence that delivers the full molten center without lingering heaviness.</li>
      <li><strong>The Small ($4.99, 620 cal):</strong> Provides substantial satiety with roughly 14 grams of natural protein from peanuts and dairy.</li>
      <li><strong>The Large ($6.49, ~1,280 cal):</strong> Best shared between family members or friends with multiple spoons.</li>
    </ul>

